        "original_id": "92743b5e-982a-5086-82d6-c781afd95607",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Jungle Book (1967 film), The Lone Ranger (2013 film), The Wheeler Dealers\n- People: Mowgli, Bagheera, Baloo, Shere Khan, Gore Verbinski, Justin Haythe, Ted Elliott, Terry Rossio, Johnny Depp, Armie Hammer, William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson, Helena Bonham Carter, Phil Harris, Martin Ransohoff, Arthur Hiller, James Garner, Lee Remick, Chill Wills, Jim Backus, Patricia Crowley\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, MGM\n- Topics: Plot, cast, production, source material\n\nFacts:\n- The Wheeler Dealers is a 1963 romantic comedy film from MGM that was produced by Martin Ransohoff, directed by Arthur Hiller, and starred James Garner and Lee Remick.\n- The Wheeler Dealers was also known in the UK as Separate Beds and featured Phil Harris, Chill Wills, Jim Backus, and Patricia Crowley.\n- The Jungle Book is a 1967 American animated musical adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Jungle Book follows Mowgli, a feral child raised by wolves in the Indian jungle, as Bagheera and Baloo try to persuade him to leave before Shere Khan arrives.\n- Phil Harris played Baloo in The Jungle Book (1967), Thomas O'Malley in The Aristocats (1970), and Little John in Robin Hood (1973).\n- The Lone Ranger is a 2013 American western action film directed by Gore Verbinski and written by Justin Haythe, Ted Elliott, and Terry Rossio.\n- The Lone Ranger was based on the radio series of the same name and starred Johnny Depp as Tonto and Armie Hammer as John Reid, the Lone Ranger.\n- The Lone Ranger relates Tonto's memories of the duo's earliest efforts to fight local villainy and bring justice to the American Old West.\n- The Lone Ranger featured William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson, and Helena Bonham Carter in supporting roles.\n- The Lone Ranger was the first theatrical film to feature the Lone Ranger and Tonto characters in more than 32 years.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
